 \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t_1)\\neq \\mathbf r(t_2), \\qquad \na < t_1< t_2 < b.\n$$\n\nFor example, curve I shown below is simple while curve II is not simple.\n\n![](images/7b/7be1bc23d37c187a642d51917d6acb846147059bc6e9978d6ccd4ed35eed8794.png)\n\nA  plane curve is said to be **closed** if its terminal point coincides with its initial point, that is, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(b)= \\mathbf r(a).\n$$\n\n![](images/4b/4b21a6e638cb8b0bae8967ba142fbfacb14349f34ff80d9359643e03ea1c1f83.png)\n\nFor example, curve III shown below is closed, while curve IV is not:\n\n![](images/85/8507fb039da42f37307ca3994cfb5ad66b288fb28d0cfd1a1a179acd2f83ae5e.png)\n\n**Watch out!** Curve III is an example of both a closed and simple curve. Notice that an example of a closed but *not* simple curve looks as shown below.\n\n![](images/86/86dcd1dc864a2f0e2ceade072ba230b8fb4fe8923189a7eed2964f6f66a67651.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173163 #edb/ref 1065 5100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173163 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "72ccdc89-4807-5abb-9f69-7e017f195c3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173163 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173171 #edb/ref 1064 "A very important (although very hard to prove) result in mathematics states the following:\n\nAny simple and closed curve divides the plane into exactly two regions, one inside the curve and one outside.\n\nBased on this fact, we can define the **orientation** of a simple closed curve as follows:\n\nA simple closed curve is **positively oriented** if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is **negatively oriented**.\n\nFor example, curve I shown below is positively oriented, while curve II is negatively oriented:\n\n![](images/95/9527dd8bdfd979a1d521ccf945e84ef9b557d67e3d89ce8f5e4f7bb8d287ee8c.png)\n\nAn alternative convenient way of looking at simple oriented curves is that a curve is positively oriented if it is traversed *counterclockwise* and it is negatively oriented if it is traversed *clockwise*." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173171 #edb/ref 1065 5165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173171 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4c2c2591-a914-53a3-9f60-6e7335d049f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173171 #edb/ref 1067 "Oriented Curves" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360855 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d7/d78da227847adf43ac482c6ea625d8978fb34463dd24d855e3369b4a4219b080.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360855 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360855 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "063d34ce-05e4-5a1c-bdbc-2a10152850a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1080 "images/cd/cd1f754fa00d1af2d8901ecc4c0cac434afb433474685fe7777d74f1703bafb2.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2eeddbc3-0c2b-51c9-a0c9-e864cef13cda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361243 #edb/ref 1080 "images/2d/2d352cf134fa7aa740d42f1de4e731cf9f53e26341a4ee3fefae809db0c8a3f1.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361243 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361243 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59405ea1-d578-52de-82ff-d38f4fd2dabb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361274 #edb/ref 1080 "images/58/58efe73124a5f0fa8824ea05d118ea92ea1b30cf950f740c9c9b5376650044bd.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361274 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361274 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "617af790-b042-53c8-b62b-12dee18a22f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361364 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d6/d64c10d8291795128189e6ce8eba748b70f8f76d746308c0209059366f5ccd6a.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7701dffc-4af8-572d-bcc4-cd6c9139e7c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361433 #edb/ref 1080 "images/79/79d7be646e819df1a5245b89c673fff1ee165bf4fe64f2b